supermox-android (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * init.d/waydroid-container: manage the LXC container as well as waydroid's
    container manager. `waydroid container start` only provides the D-Bus bus;
    the Android userspace is the container itself, so the script now brings it
    up headlessly through waydroid's own prepare_container/start_container
    (waydroid0 veth bridge, loop-mounted images, `lxc-start -F -- /init`, pid
    in /run/waydroid-container.lxc.pid) and stops both processes. The headless
    path skips the session layer's Wayland/pulse bind mounts, which only a GUI
    session needs.
  * debian/copyright: spell the license out in full (AGPL-3.0-or-later) instead
    of the bare "AGPLv3" tag.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 19:05:00 -0800

supermox-android (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: the Android layer of SuperMox. Waydroid runs a full
    Android system in an LXC container that shares the node kernel, so a
    phone (or any node) keeps its own kernel, network and storage stack
    while Android provides the userspace on top.
  * init.d/waydroid-container: sysvinit service script for
    `waydroid container start`. Upstream ships only a unit file for an
    init system we do not use, and the rootfs build drops unit files at
    install time, so nothing else started the container.
  * /etc/modules-load.d/waydroid.conf: loads binder_linux with the
    binder/hwbinder/vndbinder device arguments Android's bind mounts need.
  * /usr/sbin/supermox-android-setup: idempotent setup, pinned Lawnchair
    APK verified by sha256, --dry-run prints the whole plan.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:10:00 -0700
